SE Ranking MCP: Setup & Configuration API API integrations / MCP Server Documentation MCP Server Documentation New to SE Ranking MCP? What it does, pricing and use cases Start with 100K free credits → SE Ranking SEO MCP New · MCP Hub Explore the MCP Hub Whether you’re connecting MCP for the first time or building advanced workflows, the MCP Hub brings every useful resource into one place, so you can start simple and level up at your own pace. Setup Use cases Skills library Prompt library Blueprints Video guides Go to MCP Hub → The Model Context Protocol (MCP) server provides a standardized interface that allows any compatible AI model to access your SE Ranking and SE Visible data simply and securely. MCP server server follows the authenticated remote MCP spec, so it’s centrally hosted and managed. Connect in one click in Claude or ChatGPT , natively in Cursor and other clients, or use the mcp-remote module for clients that don’t support remote servers. What you can access Through the MCP server, your AI assistant can work with data from these SE Ranking and SE Visible products*: Data API : keyword research, backlinks, domain analysis, SERP, and more Project API : your projects, rank tracking, audits, and competitors Local Marketing API : your locations, local rankings, Google Business Profile, business listings, and reviews SE Visible API : your AI visibility projects, brands, topics, prompts, and sources *The data available to you depends on your subscription. Not every API endpoint is available through MCP. Setup is the same for every product. Use your SE Ranking account, or an API key generated in the API Dashboard of your SE Ranking or SE Visible account. Setup Instructions General Our MCP server supports Streamable HTTP transports. This transport uses OAuth 2.1 with dynamic client registration for authentication at the following address: Copy https://api.seranking.com/mcp Jump to your client: Claude · ChatGPT · Codex · Cursor · VS Code · v0 · Windsurf · Zed · Gemini CLI · Others . Sub-accounts If you’re a sub-account on a shared SE Ranking workspace, the Sign in with SE Ranking button won’t connect any tools. API access lives with the master account, not with sub-accounts. Sub-account API keys are on the way; until they’re released, use the workaround below. To connect a sub-account: Get the API key from your account administrator. In the connection dialog, choose Enter API keys manually . Paste the key when prompted. Claude Claude (Web & Desktop) Add the official SE Ranking connector and click Connect . In Claude Desktop, you can also find it under Customize → Connectors by searching for SE Ranking . Claude Code Two options. Pick one. Option A: OAuth (recommended) — opens a browser on first connect, stores the token locally, and reuses it across sessions. Copy claude mcp add --transport http se-ranking https://api.seranking.com/mcp Then run /mcp once you’ve opened a Claude Code session to go through the authentication flow. Option B: API key — skip the OAuth flow and pass your key as headers. Right for headless environments, CI runners, shared dev boxes, or when the browser handoff is awkward. Copy claude mcp add --transport http se-ranking https://api.seranking.com/mcp \ --header "X-Api-Key: *****" Grab the key from the API Dashboard in your SE Ranking or SE Visible account. Available tools depend on your subscription. ChatGPT Open the official SE Ranking plugin , click Install plugin , and sign in to authorize. You can also find it in ChatGPT under Plugins by searching for SE Ranking . Codex The setup steps for the MCP server are the same regardless of whether you use the IDE Extension or the CLI since the configuration is shared. Configuration via CLI: Run the following command in Terminal: Copy codex mcp add se-ranking --url https://api.seranking.com/mcp This will automatically prompt you to log in with your SE Ranking account and connect it to your Codex. Note: If this is the first time you are using an MCP in Codex you will need to enable the rmcp feature for this to work. Add the following into your ~/.codex/config.toml : Copy [features] experimental_use_rmcp_client = true Configuration through environment variables: 1. Open the ~/.codex/config.toml file in your preferred editor. 2. Add the following: Copy [features] experimental_use_rmcp_client = true [mcp_servers.se-ranking] url = "https://api.seranking.com/mcp" 3. Run codex mcp login se-ranking to move through the authentication flow. Cursor Add the following to .cursor/mcp.json (project) or ~/.cursor/mcp.json (global): Copy { "mcpServers": { "se-ranking": { "url": "https://api.seranking.com/mcp" } } } Cursor supports Streamable HTTP and OAuth natively. An OAuth window will open on first use to authenticate with your SE Ranking account. Visual Studio Code Copy { "mcpServers": { "se-ranking": { "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://api.seranking.com/mcp"] } } } 1. Ctrl+P / Cmd+P and search for MCP: Add Server . 2. Select Command (stdio) . 3. Enter the following configuration, and hit enter: Copy npx -y mcp-remote https://api.seranking.com/mcp 4. Enter the name SE Ranking and hit enter. 5. Activate the server using MCP: List Servers , selecting se-ranking , and selecting Start Server . v0 by Vercel To add the MCP to v0, you can install from the connections page. Windsurf 1. Ctrl+, / Cmd+, to open Windsurf settings. 2. Scroll to Cascade > MCP servers . 3. Select Add Server > Add custom server . 4. Add the following: Copy { "mcpServers": { "se-ranking": { "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://api.seranking.com/mcp"] } } } Zed Cmd+, to open Zed settings. Add the following: Copy { "context_servers": { "se-ranking": { "source": "custom", "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://api.seranking.com/mcp"], "env": {} } } } Gemini CLI Add to ~/.gemini/settings.json : Copy { "mcpServers": { "se-ranking": { "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://api.seranking.com/mcp"] } } } Save and launch Gemini CLI. Authorize when prompted. Others Hundreds of other tools now support MCP servers. You can configure them to use our MCP server with the following settings: Command: npx Arguments: -y mcp-remote https://api.seranking.com/mcp Environment: None FAQ Why am I seeing an internal server error when trying to connect? Enter the following in the Terminal to clear saved auth info: rm -rf ~/.mcp-auth then try again to connect. Additionally you may need to update to a newer version of Node if required. What happens when I connect? A browser window opens to seranking.com where you log in with your SE Ranking account and approve access. After approval, you’re redirected back to your client and the connection is established. If the window doesn’t open automatically, check your client for a URL to paste into a browser manually. How do I know the connection worked? Claude.ai / Desktop: SE Ranking moves out of Not connected and its tools become available in chats. Claude Code: Run /mcp and confirm se-ranking shows as connected and its tools are listed. Cursor, VS Code, Windsurf, Zed: The server appears as connected in the MCP panel and tools are listed. All clients: Try a prompt like “Using SE Ranking MCP, give me traffic for seranking.com in the US.” If it returns real data, it works. I’m using WSL on Windows, and seeing an error WSL can have issues with the OAuth redirect. Configure the server in your client’s Windows-side config file instead, or run the setup from PowerShell: {
  "mcpServers": {
    "se-ranking": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://api.seranking.com/mcp"]
    }
  }
} Does the MCP support Streamable HTTP? Yes, at the https://api.seranking.com/mcp endpoint. Can I authenticate with my own API key? Yes. Instead of using the interactive authentication flow, you can pass your API key in the X-Api-Key header. See Claude Code, Option B for an example. This works well for headless environments, CI runners, and shared dev boxes. A key passed this way has the same access as your account. Restricted or read-only API keys aren’t available yet. No tools appearing after connecting? Verify your SE Ranking or SE Visible account has API access at the API Dashboard. Run /mcp in Claude Code to check live connection status. Try removing and re-adding the server. If you need further assistance, contact us at [email protected] . Resources API Pricing plans MCP Hub : setup, use cases, skills, prompts, blueprints, and video guides SEO Skills : open-source Claude Skills built on SE Ranking MCP Claude Content Skills Claude Marketing Skills Model Context Protocol spec Video: SE Ranking MCP in Action See the MCP server in action in our live workshops, from first connection to automated workflows. Full live workshops One prompt, your whole stack: SE Ranking MCP Workshop Connect SE Ranking, Search Console, and GA4 in Claude, find the pages worth fixing first, and send results to Slack, email, or Linear. Watch on YouTube → From data to action: building automated SEO workflows with MCP & GA4 Connect SE Ranking to Claude in two clicks, add GA4, and run an AI visibility audit across ChatGPT, Gemini, and Google AI Overviews. Watch on YouTube → Claude Code for SEO: building a data-backed marketing agent with SE Ranking MCP Build an agent in Claude Code that turns live keyword, competitor, and AI search data into a content plan and publish-ready briefs. Watch on YouTube → Learn how SE Ranking’s API can boost your SEO! Hi! Meet our product experts! One of them will walk you through the API and show you how to get the most out of it. Enjoy a tailored demo on integra